    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nI added one new, self-contained file: `OwnerCreateAuditAdvice.java` \u2014 a small aspect that emits the create audit line **after** the derived membership fields are populated on the owner response.\n\n## Why this shape\n\nThe existing `AUDIT` line lives inside `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, but that method runs *before* the `@AfterReturning` advices (`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice` \u2192 `MembershipPoints`, and `OwnerMembershipNumberAdvice`) compute `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` on the response DTO. So the values simply aren't available at the point the controller currently logs.\n\nRather than grow `addOwner` (a method in a large controller with high surrounding complexity \u2014 the most expensive thing to touch under the cost model) and duplicate the membership-scoring logic there, I added the enrichment as a new cohesive unit with near-zero surrounding complexity:\n\n- It runs on the `addOwner` join point only (create), not `getOwner`.\n- `@Order(0)` gives it higher precedence than the default (lowest-precedence) field-populating advices, so its *after-returning* body runs **last** and observes the populated `membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber`. (My first attempt used `HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE`, which placed it ahead of Spring's `ExposeInvocationInterceptor` and threw `IllegalStateException`; `@Order(0)` avoids that while still being outermost among the real aspects.)\n- The line keeps all the fields the create audit already logged (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`) and now also carries `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`.\n\nResult: `INFO AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-02 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`, and `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` (plus the full suite) passes.\n\nOne note for your awareness: I left the controller's original `AUDIT.info` line untouched to keep structural impact low, so a create now produces two audit lines \u2014 the original three-field one and the new enriched five-field one. The enriched line satisfies the spec on its own. If you'd prefer exactly one line, I can remove the controller's line, but that means editing the large controller class (higher structural cost). Let me know your preference.",
